{"updated":"2026-10-24T16:54:44.962Z","warnings":[{"country":"united-kingdom","level":2,"type":"Rain","event":"Yellow rain warning","headline":"Heavy rain brings a high likelihood of moderate impacts from surface water flooding.","description":"Heavy rain in association with Storm Boelo is expected to lead to surface water flooding in places. 25-30mm is expected widely across the warning area during this time, with a few places such as upland areas seeing 50-60mm, and some of this perhaps falling within 6 hours. Rain will ease for a time through the evening, but this will be followed by another intense band of heavy rain following in from the west, before the whole system clears away eastward to bring a clear night with a few scattered showers following on.\n\nFor further details see https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/weather/warnings-and-advice/uk-warnings","instruction":"Give yourself the best chance of avoiding delays by checking road conditions if driving, or bus and train timetables, amending your travel plans if necessary.\n\nPeople cope better with power cuts when they have prepared for them in advance. It's easy to do; consider gathering torches and batteries, a mobile phone power pack and other essential items.\n\nCheck if your property could be at risk of floo","sender":"UK Met Office","web":"https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/weather/warnings-and-advice/uk-warnings","onset":"2026-10-24T10:00:00.000Z","expires":"2026-10-24T22:00:00.000Z","areas":["London & South East England | North West England | South West England | Wales | West Midlands | Yorkshire & Humber"],"polys":[[[-6.62,49.69,-6.69,49.77,-6.72,50.01,-6.64,50.32,-6.56,50.5,-5.43,52.51,-5.1,53.04,-4.32,54.1,-3.96,54.51,-3.78,54.67,-3.59,54.78,-3.16,54.94,-2.86,54.96,-2.77,54.94,-2.61,54.84,-2.34,54.4,-2.19,53.87,-2.18,53.64,-2.24,53.48,-2.4,53.39,-2.77,53.32,-2.92,53.26,-3,53.18,-3.1,52.96,-3.14,52.49,-3.08,52.13,-2.92,51.81,-2.71,51.6,-2.53,51.49,-2.19,51.38,-1.48,51.28,-0.1,51.24,0.31,51.26,1.44,51.44,1.5,51.